  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday Night through Sunday)\nIssued at 1139 PM CDT Sun Oct 11 2026\n\nLow level moisture will increase Monday night and Tuesday \nresulting in overnight low temperatures more commonly seen in \nJuly than October. Record warm low temperatures will likely be set\nTuesday and Wednesday in many locations, with additional cloud\ncover Tuesday possibly keeping afternoon highs just below record\nlevels, although it will be close.\n\nA frontal boundary sagging south to near the Oklahoma/Kansas\nborder combined with an upper trough over the western U.S.\nejecting out into the central plains will result in multiple\nrounds of showers and thunderstorms Tuesday night through\nThursday, especially from northeast Oklahoma into far northwest\nArkansas. Locally heavy rainfall will likely occur, and a few\nstrong to severe storms will also be possible. A stronger cold \nfront will surge south across the area Thursday or Thursday night,\nwith the precipitation tapering off and ending in its wake.\n\nMuch cooler and drier weather will prevail behind the front Friday\nthrough next weekend, with below normal temperatures expected for\nthe first time in a couple months.",
